# Lakewood IT Hotline — API examples
# Use with VS Code REST Client, or copy curl commands below.
# Base URL — adjust if needed
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Auth me (business or provider JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Register business (use for dev login — seed passwords are placeholders)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/business/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rosa's Corner Market",
  "email": "rosa.test@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "address": "123 Lakewood Ave SE, Atlanta, GA 30315",
  "type": "market",
  "lat": 33.7418,
  "lng": -84.3852
}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/business/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rosa.test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Available providers near point
GET {{baseUrl}}/providers/available/count?lat=33.753&lng=-84.390

### Current business profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/business/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update business profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/business/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rosa's Corner Market",
  "address": "123 Lakewood Ave SE, Atlanta, GA 30315"
}

### Create ticket (schedules escalation check via RQ)
# @name createTicket
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "pos",
  "severity": "urgent",
  "problemReport": "Register 2 keeps freezing during lunch rush. Screen goes white.",
  "photoKeys": []
}

### List my tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ticket detail (includes presigned photo URLs)
@ticketId = {{createTicket.response.body.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Upload photo to ticket (multipart)
POST {{baseUrl}}/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ticket_id"

{{ticketId}}
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="upload_type"

problem
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="problem.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/local/photo.jpg
------Boundary--

### List messages on ticket
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Post message (business)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Can you come today? We're turning customers away."
}

### Cancel ticket (only before complete/confirmed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cancelReason": "Issue resolved internally"
}

### Confirm ticket (only when status=complete — set manually in DB for testing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/6/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "business_rating": 1
}

###
# curl quick reference
#
# curl http://localhost:5001/health
#
# curl -X POST http://localhost:5001/auth/business/register \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"name":"Test Shop","email":"test@example.com","password":"password123","address":"1 Main St","type":"market","lat":33.75,"lng":-84.39}'
#
# TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:5001/auth/business/login \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"email":"test@example.com","password":"password123"}' | python3 -c "import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['token'])")
#
# curl http://localhost:5001/business/me -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
#
# curl "http://localhost:5001/providers/available/count?lat=33.753&lng=-84.390"
#
# curl -X POST http://localhost:5001/tickets \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"type":"pos","severity":"urgent","problemReport":"Register frozen"}'

# ============================================================
# PROVIDER (IT worker) endpoints
# ============================================================

@providerToken = {{providerLogin.response.body.token}}
@providerToken2 = {{providerLogin2.response.body.token}}

### Register provider
# @name providerRegister
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/provider/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fname": "Test",
  "lname": "Tech",
  "email": "tech.test@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "+14045559901",
  "lat": 33.7495,
  "lng": -84.3835,
  "skills": ["pos", "network"],
  "vouchedBy": "Rev. James Holloway",
  "vouchedRelationship": "community referral"
}

### Provider login
# @name providerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/provider/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "tech.test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Provider profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/provider/me
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### Update provider profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/provider/me
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service_radius_m": 10000,
  "skills": ["pos", "network", "equipment"]
}

### Turn on availability ("taking calls")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/provider/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "availability": true,
  "avail_start_time": "08:00",
  "avail_end_time": "18:00"
}

### List open tickets near provider
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/open?lat=33.753&lng=-84.390
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### View open ticket detail (before claim)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### Claim ticket (atomic)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/claim
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### Update journey status — en route
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "en_route"
}

### Update journey status — on site
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "on_site"
}

### Provider message
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "On site now — checking the register."
}

### Complete ticket (provider close-out)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completionReport": "Replaced failing USB hub and updated drivers.",
  "amount_charged": 125.00,
  "provider_rating": 1,
  "parts": "USB hub",
  "apprenticeAssisted": true,
  "apprenticeName": "Jordan Lee"
}

### Upload completion photo (provider)
POST {{baseUrl}}/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary2

------Boundary2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ticket_id"

{{ticketId}}
------Boundary2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="upload_type"

completion
------Boundary2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="done.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/local/photo.jpg
------Boundary2--

### Twilio inbound webhook (simulate YES reply)
POST {{baseUrl}}/twilio/inbound
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

From=%2B14045550103&Body=YES

# ============================================================
# CLAIM RACE TEST — only one provider should win (409 for loser)
# Run from shell after creating an open ticket:
#
#   # 1) Register + approve two providers in DB (status='approved', availability=1)
#   # 2) Create open ticket as business → note TICKET_ID
#   # 3) Run both claims in parallel:
#
#   TOKEN_A=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:5001/auth/provider/login \
#     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#     -d '{"email":"tech.a@example.com","password":"password123"}' \
#     | python3 -c "import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['token'])")
#   TOKEN_B=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:5001/auth/provider/login \
#     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#     -d '{"email":"tech.b@example.com","password":"password123"}' \
#     | python3 -c "import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['token'])")
#   TICKET_ID=1
#   curl -s -o /tmp/claim_a.json -w "%{http_code}\n" -X POST \
#     "http://localhost:5001/tickets/${TICKET_ID}/claim" \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN_A" &
#   curl -s -o /tmp/claim_b.json -w "%{http_code}\n" -X POST \
#     "http://localhost:5001/tickets/${TICKET_ID}/claim" \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN_B" &
#   wait
#   echo "A:" $(cat /tmp/claim_a.json)
#   echo "B:" $(cat /tmp/claim_b.json)
#   # Expect one 200 and one 409 with {"error":"already claimed"}
# ============================================================

### Register second provider (for race test setup)
# @name providerRegister2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/provider/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fname": "Race",
  "lname": "TechB",
  "email": "tech.b@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "+14045559902",
  "lat": 33.7495,
  "lng": -84.3835,
  "skills": ["pos"]
}

### Second provider login
# @name providerLogin2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/provider/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "tech.b@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Race claim — provider A (run A and B back-to-back quickly, or use shell script above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/1/claim
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### Race claim — provider B (expect 409 if A won)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/1/claim
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken2}}

